!!! archon/engine/smoke.mat
!!! End-to-end smoke test for the scanning engine.
!!!
!!! Scans one sample target with three rules drawn from three different
!!! categories (code, security, permission) and asserts the finding count and
!!! the highest severity through the machine-readable report line.

book archon.engine.smoke

read everything from ny.lang.core
read everything from ny.lang.text
read everything from archon.model.severity
read everything from archon.model.confidence
read everything from archon.model.category
read everything from archon.model.location
read everything from archon.model.finding
read everything from archon.model.rule
read everything from archon.model.target
read everything from archon.model.report
read everything from archon.engine.scanner
read everything from archon.engine.patterns

main returns number begin paragraph
    !!! A small mixed sample: one issue per rule.
    value sample as text is begin text
        char password[32];
        strcpy(buffer, input);
        chmod 777 /data;
    end text

    variable rules as array of knowledge-rule is []
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "code.unsafe-copy", title being "Unbounded string copy", needle being "strcpy(", guidance being "Use a bounded copy.", level being severity.High, certainty being confidence.Likely, domain being category.Code) to rules
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "sec.hardcoded-secret", title being "Hard-coded secret", needle being "password", guidance being "Move secrets out of source.", level being severity.Critical, certainty being confidence.Speculative, domain being category.Security) to rules
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "perm.world-writable", title being "World-writable path", needle being "chmod 777", guidance being "Grant the narrowest permission.", level being severity.High, certainty being confidence.Likely, domain being category.Permission) to rules

    value target is build scan-target with label being "engine/sample.c", kind being "code", content being sample

    value findings is scan with target being target, rules being rules
    value summary is summarize with target being target, findings being findings, rules-applied being (the length of rules)

    repeat for each item in findings
        say (finding-summary with item being item)
    end repeat
    say (report-summary with summary being summary)

    give 0
end paragraph
